    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="9c7fb74b-d3c1-5878-9334-3239df2352af" activityNameId="fd8d8df9-4876-56ad-9b9f-1a0159de727d" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, medium voltage, residual mix</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, medium voltage, residual mix
This dataset describes the transformation from high to medium voltage as well as the transmission of electricity at medium voltage.; UUID:982def76-ac2d-31f8-863e-345a725af988
Included are the electricity production in CH, the transmission network and direct SF6-emissions to air. Electricity losses during medium-voltage transmission and transformation from high-voltage are accounted for.
Location: Data apply to untracked electricity supplied in "&amp;T53&amp;". Geographical classification according to IEA.Transmission network, losses and emissions are taken from Itten, Frischknecht and Stucki (2014): LCI of Electricity Mixes and Grid.
Technology: Average technology used to transmit and distribute electricity. Includes underground and overhead lines, as well as air-, vacuum- and SF6-insulated high-to-medium voltage switching stations. Electricity production according to related datasets
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: 
Sampling: Statistical data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_982def76-ac2d-31f8-863e-345a725af988.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
